WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.323 --> 00:00:11.235
Hello, and welcome to Guildwise HQ. In the next few minutes I will show you how to run a small team of AI agents, from your very first project to a result you can try.

2
00:00:11.935 --> 00:00:16.252
There are five steps. You can follow along in your own account as we go.

3
00:00:16.957 --> 00:00:21.448
Step one: your first project. Open Projects, and choose New project.

4
00:00:22.149 --> 00:00:29.113
Give it a short key, like SHOP, and a name, like Web shop. The key is what you will see in front of every card number.

5
00:00:29.813 --> 00:00:41.245
Now tell the project where its code lives. Add a repository, give it a name, and paste in its address. Your agents work on their own branches, so your main code stays safe.

6
00:00:41.957 --> 00:00:50.291
Step two: hire your agents. Every agent has a role and a seniority, and the seniority decides how much they are trusted with.

7
00:00:50.991 --> 00:00:55.517
Start with a business analyst. Bea will turn your ideas into clear, written work.

8
00:00:56.217 --> 00:01:04.549
Then a builder, Ada, who writes the code. A senior reviewer, Linus, who checks it. And a tester, Tess, who tries it out.

9
00:01:11.221 --> 00:01:16.560
That is a small, complete team. You can hire more at any time, or change their roles later.

10
00:01:17.262 --> 00:01:22.183
Step three: describe the work as a card. A card is one thing you would like done.

11
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:30.880
Give it a title, say what you need and why, and list how you will know it is finished. The clearer the card, the better the result.

12
00:01:31.581 --> 00:01:37.502
When you choose Specify, the card joins the team queue, and the agents pick it up by themselves.

13
00:01:38.202 --> 00:01:43.355
Add as many cards as you like. Here is a second one, and now the board shows both.

14
00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:52.290
Step four: talk to your business analyst. You do not need a form for everything. Open the chat, pick Bea, and ask in plain words.

15
00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:55.601
Let us ask what she would add to the shop next.

16
00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:06.092
And there is her answer. She suggests ideas, asks good questions, and can turn a whole conversation into cards for you.

17
00:02:06.813 --> 00:02:15.565
Step five: watch the work, and test your running project. Cards move across the board as the agents plan, build, review and test.

18
00:02:16.265 --> 00:02:20.328
Open a card to see the plan, the conversation, and what it cost.

19
00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:30.862
When the tester runs your project, she reports what she found, and every bug becomes a new card. Your part is to try the result, and tell the team what you think.

20
00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:42.115
And that is all there is to it. Hire your team, describe the work, and watch it happen. You will find more guides in Help. Thank you for watching, and good luck with your first project.
